<title>RUSSIA: Russian Jan-Aug trade surplus widens to $23.61 bln.</title>
<headline>Russian Jan-Aug trade surplus widens to $23.61 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia posted a trade surplus of $23.61 billion in the first eight months of this year from a $21.24 billion surplus in the same period of 1995, Interfax said on Friday quoting the State Customs Committee.</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN MERCHANDISE TRADE   Jan-Aug 96    Jan-Aug 95</p>
<p>    exports			     44.798	 42.595</p>
<p>    imports			     21.193	 21.357</p>
<p>    trade balance		    +23.606	+21.238</p>
<p>Notes -- Figures in billion dollars, FOB. Data are for trade with Russia's &quot;far abroad&quot;, excluding former Soviet states and imports by small private traders. Including trade with former Soviet republics, the surplus widened to $24.02 billion from $22.46 billion.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
